## Code Unit Prioritization (Phase 1)

[This section guides Phase 1 "Coverage Mode" - systematic analysis of each component.]

Target medium-sized units: [List the types of code units to analyze. Examples:
- For ZK circuits: "constraint generation functions, circuit gadgets, witness calculators"
- For cryptography: "signature functions, key derivation functions, encryption/decryption routines"
- For blockchain nodes: "consensus handlers, block processors, transaction validators, p2p message handlers"
- For smart contracts: "contracts, protocol modules, library functions"
- For wallets: "key derivation modules, transaction signers, address generators, mnemonic handlers"]

Prioritize components:
[List 3-5 criteria for which components are most critical to analyze first. Examples for crypto/blockchain:]

[For ZK circuits:]
- Handling witness inputs and public inputs
- Performing field arithmetic and constraint generation
- Implementing cryptographic primitives (hashing, signatures)
- Managing circuit composition and gadget integration

[For blockchain nodes:]
- Handling consensus-critical state transitions
- Processing blocks and transactions
- Validating cryptographic proofs and signatures
- Managing p2p message handling and DOS protection

[For smart contracts:]
- Handling asset transfers or monetary value
- Implementing access control and authorization
- Managing upgradeable proxies or admin functions
- Integrating with external oracles or bridges

[For wallets:]
- Deriving and storing private keys
- Constructing and signing transactions
- Handling mnemonic generation and recovery
- Managing multi-signature or threshold schemes

[**Tip:** Focus on components that handle cryptographic operations, value transfer, or consensus-critical logic.]

