## Vulnerability Categories (Phase 1 - Coverage)

[List the specific vulnerability types relevant to your domain. This guides systematic vulnerability scanning during Phase 1.]

Look for these vulnerability types during systematic analysis:

[For ZK-SNARK circuits:]
- Under-constrained circuits (missing constraints)
- Arithmetic overflow/underflow in field operations
- Constraint system bugs (unsatisfiable or trivially satisfiable)
- Soundness violations (accepting invalid proofs)
- Completeness violations (rejecting valid proofs)
- Witness malleability (multiple valid witnesses)
- Trusted setup compromise vectors
- Circuit composition errors

[For ECDSA/Cryptography:]
- Weak randomness in nonce generation
- Signature malleability issues
- Timing side-channels in constant-time operations
- Key reuse or improper key derivation
- Insecure curve parameters or point validation
- Missing point-at-infinity checks
- Improper hash-to-curve implementations
- Side-channel leakage (cache timing, power analysis)

[For blockchain nodes:]
- Consensus safety violations (forking, double-spend)
- Liveness failures (chain halts, deadlocks)
- P2P DoS vectors (resource exhaustion, amplification)
- State corruption or invalid state transitions
- Block/transaction validation bypasses
- Memory exhaustion in mempool or state
- Eclipse attacks or peer isolation
- Reorg handling vulnerabilities

[For smart contracts:]
- Reentrancy vulnerabilities
- Access control issues
- Integer overflow/underflow
- Oracle manipulation
- Front-running and MEV risks
- Logic errors in state transitions
- Proxy upgrade vulnerabilities
- Missing validation of external calls

[For crypto wallets:]
- Private key leakage or insecure storage
- Weak key derivation (predictable keys)
- Transaction signature malleability
- Replay attacks across chains
- Mnemonic entropy issues
- Insecure randomness for key generation
- Missing transaction validation
- Address validation bypasses

[**Tip:** Research domain-specific vulnerability databases - for crypto/blockchain see: DeFi exploit databases, ZK security audits, consensus bug bounties, cryptographic implementation CVEs.]

