## Node Type Terminology

[Define what types of nodes (code entities) Hound should create in the analysis graphs. This helps structure the graph properly.]

**Preferred node types:**

[For ZK-SNARK circuits:]
- Circuit-level nodes (e.g., "circuit_MerkleProof", "circuit_Poseidon")
- Gadget/template nodes (e.g., "gadget_RangeCheck", "template_EdDSAVerifier")
- Signal nodes (e.g., "signal_publicInput", "signal_intermediateHash")
- Constraint nodes (only when analyzing specific constraint bugs)

[For ECDSA/Cryptography:]
- Function-level nodes (e.g., "func_sign_ecdsa", "func_verify_signature")
- Primitive nodes (e.g., "primitive_sha256", "primitive_scalar_mult")
- Key material nodes (e.g., "privkey_generated", "pubkey_derived")
- Operation nodes (e.g., "op_point_add", "op_mod_inverse")

[For blockchain nodes:]
- Function-level nodes (e.g., "func_validateBlock", "func_processTransaction")
- Handler nodes (e.g., "handler_p2p_block", "handler_consensus_vote")
- State nodes (e.g., "state_accountBalances", "state_blockchainHead")
- Validator nodes (e.g., "validator_checkProof", "validator_verifySignature")

[For smart contracts:]
- Function-level nodes (e.g., "func_transfer", "func_mint")
- Storage-level nodes (e.g., "storage_balances", "storage_owner")
- Modifier nodes (e.g., "modifier_onlyOwner", "modifier_nonReentrant")
